# Origin the typed API client sends requests to (e.g. https://api.example.com).
# When empty, requests fall back to the current origin (window.location.origin).
# The recommended topology is same-origin in every environment, so this should
# stay empty unless the frontend and API are intentionally split across hosts:
#
# - Local development: leave empty. The Vite dev server proxies /api requests
#   to the local FastAPI service (see vite.config.ts).
# - Docker: leave empty when the frontend and API are exposed through the same
#   reverse proxy. Set a value only when the API is intentionally hosted on a
#   separate origin.
# - Kubernetes (dev and prod): default to same-origin routing behind one
#   Ingress per namespace, and leave this empty. Use a full origin only if the
#   frontend and API are intentionally deployed on different hosts.
#
# Never set this to a path like /api or /api/v1 (not a full origin): the
# generated OpenAPI client (src/api/schema.gen.ts) already contains absolute
# paths such as /api/v1/campaigns, so a path prefix here would duplicate it.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
